  "summary": "Explain why the compiler-to-ledger-to-knowledge-graph proof matters and correct stale README boundaries.",
  "why": "The first publication stated the milestone accurately but led with machinery rather than the problem it solves. The revised page distinguishes the trivial three-record result from the provenance and replay proof, explains the exact work in plain language, exposes supplied-check and Python-runtime limits, separates the fixture from the protocol, and repairs six stale or misleading README claims found by direct code and test inspection."
